    "title": "Seasons in Canada",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "In Canada, there are four seasons: spring, summer, autumn and winter. The weather is very different in each season."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Winter is long and very cold. In many places the temperature is minus twenty degrees. There is a lot of snow, and the lakes freeze. People wear thick coats, hats and gloves. Children go to school on snowy days, and many people enjoy skiing and ice hockey."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Spring starts in March, but it is still cold at first. In April the snow melts, and flowers begin to grow. It rains a lot in spring. Summer is warm and sunny. In July the temperature is about twenty-five degrees. Many families go camping near lakes and swim in the water."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Autumn is the most beautiful season for many people. The leaves on the trees change colour from green to red, orange and yellow. The weather is cool, and the days become shorter. In October, families eat a big dinner together to say thank you for the food. Then winter comes again."
      }
    ]
  },
